<title>MEXICO: Latin American apparent steel consumption - ILAFA.</title>
<headline>Latin American apparent steel consumption - ILAFA.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latin American Insitute of Iron and Steel (ILAFA) outlined here at the Latin American Steel Congress apparent consumption of raw steel by country in the region. A table follows with a breakdown in 1000s of tonnes. The figure for 1996 is preliminary.</p>
<p>  Country	 1994     1995     1996   %Chnge 96/95</p>
<p>  Argentina     3,486    3,165    3,450	9.0</p>
<p>  Brazil	 13,801   13,786   14,478	5.0</p>
<p>  Chile	   1,464    1,820    1,930	6.0</p>
<p>  Colombia	1,959    2,065    2,190	6.1</p>
<p>  Mexico	 12,739    7,300    7,953	8.9</p>
<p>  Peru		871	920    1,000	8.7</p>
<p>  Venezuela     2,382    2,271    2,271	0.0</p>
<p>  Others	  2,455    2,400    2,158    -10.1</p>
<p>  Total	  39,157   33,727   35,430	5.1</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530</p>
